WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.775
Try it.

2
00:00:00.775 --> 00:00:04.137
Lab 1 runs in the ansible
folder of the examples,

3
00:00:04.137 --> 00:00:06.637
on a disposable Linux control node.

4
00:00:06.637 --> 00:00:09.725
Nothing signs in to Azure
or contacts a server.

5
00:00:09.725 --> 00:00:13.612
Step one installs the pinned
collections from a reviewed source,

6
00:00:13.612 --> 00:00:17.212
and then points every outbound
request at a dead local proxy.

7
00:00:17.212 --> 00:00:20.524
The results on these slides
are the chapter's Lab 1 text:

8
00:00:20.524 --> 00:00:23.911
the authors didn't re-run the
Ansible steps for this path,

9
00:00:23.911 --> 00:00:27.812
because they download from Galaxy
and need a Linux control node.

10
00:00:27.812 --> 00:00:32.878
Step two shows what the CMDB becomes:
four candidates, app oh two,

11
00:00:32.878 --> 00:00:38.237
aws oh one, web oh one and win oh one,
and five servers Ansible patches.

12
00:00:38.237 --> 00:00:42.062
Aws oh one's tags carry
both owners as Ansible.

13
00:00:42.062 --> 00:00:46.374
Step three runs Microsoft's
role, unchanged, in check mode.

14
00:00:46.374 --> 00:00:49.950
It fails at Get azcmagent
status, because there's no agent.

15
00:00:49.950 --> 00:00:54.007
Run it again verbose, and it shows
the agent installed fact as true,

16
00:00:54.007 --> 00:00:56.862
because check mode
skipped the version check.

17
00:00:56.862 --> 00:00:59.140
That's the dry run the role can't do.
